    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Title: CloudScale Core API - Getting Started Guide\n\n---\n\nWelcome to the CloudScale Core API. This guide will help you get started with basic operations. Follow the steps below to authenticate, make your first request, and handle common errors effectively.\n\n### 1. Authentication (Using Bearer Tokens)\n\nTo interact with CloudScale Core API, your requests must be authenticated. We use secure Bearer tokens for this purpose.\n- Obtain a Bearer token by requesting your API credentials from your CloudScale account.\n- Once you have your token, include it in the Authorization header of your requests. Format it as follows:\n  ```\n  Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN\n  ```\n- Set up your environment with your token:\n  ```\n  export CLOUDSCALE_API_KEY=YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN\n  ```\n\n### 2. Making Your First GET Request to /v1/status\n\nNow that you're authenticated, it's time to interact with the API. Let's check the service status with a simple GET request.\n- Execute the following curl command:\n  ```\n  curl --request GET \\\n  --url 'https://api.cloudscale.com/v1/status' \\\n  --header \"Authorization: Bearer $CLOUDSCALE_API_KEY\"\n  ```",
      "source": "target",
